  "name": "loss_logsigmoid_000_cost_tuned_scale",
  "intuition": "The loss uses a logsigmoid on x = alpha*scale*(lpw-lpl) - 0.1*gap with clamping to [-20, 20]. With limited proxy pairing budget, too-large scale can push x into saturation where gradients vanish (especially when (lpw-lpl) has moderate magnitude), while too-small scale under-separates winners/losers. I slightly reduce `scale` from 1.95 to 1.35 to keep x more often in the high-gradient region of logsigmoid given the fixed -0.1*gap term, improving stability and learning signal without changing the loss form.",
  "pseudocode": "x = clamp(alpha*scale*(lpw-lpl) - 0.1*detach(cost_b-cost_a), -20, 20); loss = -logsigmoid(x); return mean(weight*loss if weight else loss)",
  "hyperparams": {
    "scale": 1.35
  },
  "operators_used": [
