{
  "name": "consensus_logsigmoid_margin_costsafe_v0",
  "intuition": "All parents share the same stable core: a pairwise preference objective using -logsigmoid of a scaled log-probability difference (lpw-lpl) with clamping for numeric stability and optional example weights. A consensus-safe improvement is to add a small positive margin inside the logits to encourage separation even when lpw≈lpl, while keeping the behavior identical in the large-gap regime due to clamping. Additionally, when cost signals are present, we subtract a detached cost_gap term (as seen in the cost-aware parents) to softly discourage preferring options that are more costly, without allowing gradients to flow through the costs.",
  "pseudocode": "d = lpw - lpl; gap = detach(cost_b - cost_a) if present else 0; x = clamp(alpha*scale*d + margin - cost_coef*gap, -20, 20); loss = -logsigmoid(x); if weight: loss*=weight; return mean(loss)",
  "hyperparams": {
    "scale": 1.3,
    "margin": 0.05,
    "cost_coef": 0.1
  },
  "operators_used": [
    "logsigmoid",
    "clamp"
  ],
  "code": "def generated_loss(batch, model_output, extra):\n    lpw = batch['log_prob_w']\n    lpl = batch['log_prob_l']\n    weight = batch.get('weight', None)\n\n    hp = extra.get('hyperparams', {})\n    alpha = float(extra.get('alpha', hp.get('alpha', 1.0)))\n    scale = float(hp.get('scale', 1.3))\n    margin = float(hp.get('margin', 0.05))\n    cost_coef = float(hp.get('cost_coef', 0.1))\n\n    d = lpw - lpl\n\n    # Optional cost shaping: detach to avoid gradients through cost features.\n    if ('cost_a' in batch) and ('cost_b' in batch):\n        gap = (batch['cost_b'] - batch['cost_a']).detach()\n    else:\n        gap = 0.0\n\n    x = alpha * scale * d + margin - cost_coef * gap\n    x = ops.clamp(x, -20.0, 20.0)\n    loss = -ops.logsigmoid(x)\n\n    if weight is not None:\n        loss = loss * weight\n\n    return loss.mean()",
  "theoretical_basis": "Pairwise logistic (Bradley-Terry) preference loss on log-probability differences, with clamping for numerical stability; optional detached auxiliary cost shaping acts as a fixed logit shift; a small margin encourages separation when logits are near zero.",
  "implementation_hint": {
    "expects": {
      "batch": [
        "log_prob_w",
        "log_prob_l"
      ],
      "optional_batch": [
        "weight",
        "cost_a",
        "cost_b"
      ],
      "extra": [
        "hyperparams",
        "alpha"
      ]
    }
  }
}

{
  "name": "consensus_logsigmoid_margin_costsafe_v0_m3",
  "intuition": "Stabilize the pairwise logistic preference loss by (1) explicitly declaring required expects keys so the static gate can validate inputs, and (2) adding shape/broadcast-safe defaults for optional fields (weight, costs) without Python loops. Keep the core semantics: minimize -logsigmoid of a scaled log-prob gap, with small margin and clamping to avoid overflow; cost shaping remains a detached logit shift so it cannot introduce gradient instability.",
  "pseudocode": "require log_prob_w, log_prob_l; d=lpw-lpl; gap=detach(cost_b-cost_a) if provided else 0; x=clamp(alpha*scale*d+margin-cost_coef*gap,-20,20); loss=-logsigmoid(x); if weight: loss*=clamp_min(weight,0); return mean(loss)",
