{
  "name": "loss_logsigmoid_005_cost_crossover_m3_safe_keys",
  "intuition": "Stabilize and satisfy static expects by supporting multiple common key aliases for the winner/loser log-probs (log_prob_w/log_prob_l as well as log_prob_chosen/log_prob_rejected and chosen_logps/rejected_logps). Keep the loss purely pairwise -logsigmoid on a clamped margin for numerical stability. Apply optional cost-gap shaping only when both cost fields exist, detach it to avoid gradient instability, and normalize weights safely (clamp nonnegative, divide by sum+eps) to prevent negative or exploding effective scaling.",
  "pseudocode": "lpw,lpl = get_pair_logps_with_aliases(batch)
x = alpha*scale*(lpw-lpl)
if cost_a and cost_b: x = x - cost_coef*detach(cost_b-cost_a)
x = clamp(x,-20,20)
loss = -logsigmoid(x)
if weight: w = clamp(weight,0,inf); loss = sum(w*loss)/(sum(w)+eps) else mean(loss)",
