  "intuition": "The joint preference gate failed because gradients w.r.t. log_prob_w/log_prob_l were often overwhelmed or flipped by the additive cost adjustment, reducing the pass rate for the expected direction checks. I fixed this by (1) making the core signal strictly the pairwise logit gap (log_prob_w - log_prob_l) and (2) incorporating cost only as a small, bounded multiplicative attenuation on that core gap rather than an additive term. This preserves the correct monotonic gradient directions (dL/dlog_prob_w < 0, dL/dlog_prob_l > 0 for typical cases) while still letting higher cost gaps reduce the strength of the update. I also clamp the preference logit to avoid saturation and keep gradients stable across batches.",
  "pseudocode": "gap = log_prob_w - log_prob_l; cgap = cost_b - cost_a; attn = 1 - cost_coef * sigmoid(cgap); x = alpha*scale*attn*gap; loss = -logsigmoid(clamp(x,-20,20))",
