{
  "name": "loss_logsigmoid_cost_tanh_softcap_alpha_guard_v2",
  "intuition": "The failure came from calling ops.tanh() on Python floats (alpha and hyperparams were cast to float), but ops.* expects Tensor inputs. I fixed this by keeping alpha and all hyperparameters as tensors on the same device/dtype as the batch tensors, using pure tensor arithmetic for alpha soft-bounding and logit soft-capping. This preserves the intended behavior (DPO-style -logsigmoid on a preference logit with bounded cost shaping) while avoiding any scalar-to-tensor type errors and remaining fully vectorized.",
  "pseudocode": "d = log_prob_w - log_prob_l
cost_gap = cost_b - cost_a
alpha_eff = alpha_cap * tanh(alpha / alpha_cap)
x_raw = alpha_eff*scale*d - cost_coef*tanh(cost_gap)
x = x_cap * tanh(x_raw / x_cap)
loss = -logsigmoid(x)
return mean(loss*weight if weight else loss)",
